today we're gonna talk about one that's slightly unusual

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:38.580
that does see quite a lot of use in research in academia

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:39.780
uhm. and.

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:40.800
...in...

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:43.600
client science and things like that where I obviously do a bit of work.

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:45.320
I mean that's called "space carving"

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:49.540
"Space carving" is the idea of, in a sense, of starting with a big lump of clay

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:51.780
Working out where you know your object is not

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:53.300
and cutting that clay away

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:56.640
until you get something that kind of resembles what you know your object is supposed to be

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:59.520
except, its based only on what you can see in 2-dimensional images

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:02.240
so a good example would be if I give you this, if I show you this..

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:03.300
alright what... what's that?

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:04.000
Offscreen: er. ok?

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:05.820
Thats a serious. its not... its not a trick question

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:09.260
offscreen Narrator: Okay well that's obviously...a..a mug. Its a cylinder with some ..uh

00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:11.640
(Interrupting) It is a mug, right !?! 
...Its a cylinder with a handle on it

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:13.120
which is...
...I don't know what the shape of that is

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:13.660
Right?

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:15.057
But the thing is you can't absol-

00:02:15.057 --> 00:02:16.200
you can't acutally be sure.

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:18.320
ok you've only got one camera. You're looking at it from this direction.

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:20.980
This mug could go off for one meter.. backwards!

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:22.160
into this wall.

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:24.460
and you wouldn't absolutely be sure that it didn't do that

00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:26.760
apart from your intuition about what it is.

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:27.300
ok?

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:29.360
and, and the fact that you're a human. You know its a mug.

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:30.640
Offscreen narrator: I mean, thats..(stammering) .. sorry

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:33.840
its just that because i'm on the handheld and not on the tripod I can move side to side...

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:34.960
(interrupting) You can move side to side, ok?

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:37.640
So one of the ways we work out what an object shape is

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:40.280
truly, we move around it and see it from other angles

00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:43.340
ok? or we rotate the object and find out it isn't in fact a meter long

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:44.780
because I would have just hit myself in the head!
(offscreen laughter)

00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:46.040
Ok? ...so!

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:49.200
but the point is that until we see it from a different angle we can't be absolutely sure

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:50.780
now in .. on a computer...

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:51.920
that's more true, even

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:53.740
because they can't intuit anything

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:54.780
they..

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:55.500
so ...

00:02:56.040 --> 00:03:00.440
they say: "well? its a square box with a 'lil circle on the end of it"

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:02.280
and that's all they can tell us!

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:03.980
ok? they can't tell us what shape it is,

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:04.760
they can't tell us that its hollow

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:06.620
uh. or anything else

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:08.880
because uh.. how?... how would they know?

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:10.800
how would they know that it isn't longer this way?

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:11.300
ok?

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:13.280
unless we start to build in some sort of rules.

00:03:13.480 --> 00:03:15.320
so, what space carving does

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:16.000
is

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:17.000
look at this mug

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:17.720
and

00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:19.920
try and carve a piece of clay in that shape

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:20.700
ok?

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:22.740
but under the assumption that it could go back here

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:23.600
right?

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:25.280
then we turn it and go: "oh! it doesn't."

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:26.320
and cut that bit off

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:28.500
and then we turn it again. And we cut that bit off.

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:31.340
and we keep doing this until we cut off as much as we can

00:03:31.340 --> 00:03:34.220
the more views we get the better that..that the..

00:03:34.220 --> 00:03:35.260
...the result.

